WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.600
Good morning, teacher and classmates.

00:00:02.600 --> 00:00:05.900
My name is Mai Như Ý, class 11A9, and this is my partner.

00:00:06.250 --> 00:00:08.600
My name is Nguyễn Thành Đạt, in class 11A9.

00:00:08.900 --> 00:00:12.400
Today, we are excited to present a vision

00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:15.850
of the ideal living space for humanity in the coming decades.

00:00:16.350 --> 00:00:19.800
That's right. Welcome to our Green City of the Future model,

00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:23.300
where modern technology doesn't clash with nature,

00:00:23.300 --> 00:00:26.500
but blends with it to protect the environment and improve our lives.

00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:28.500
Let's explore how this amazing city works.

00:00:28.600 --> 00:00:34.200
Beneath the surface, underground water flows

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:39.500
to run a mini hydropower station and a geothermal plant

00:00:39.500 --> 00:00:43.000
that taps into the Earth's natural heat.

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:46.400
This keeps the city self-sufficient with zero harmful emissions.

00:00:46.600 --> 00:00:53.100
Beyond clean electricity, the transport system is 100% eco-friendly.

00:00:53.400 --> 00:00:59.050
High above the streets, an elevated train provides fast transit and prevents traffic jams.

00:00:59.450 --> 00:01:02.200
Down on the ground, residents use electric cars and bicycles,

00:01:02.650 --> 00:01:06.500
keeping the air fresh, clean, and quiet.

00:01:06.500 --> 00:01:10.800
And especially, we also provide a flying car, as you can see.

00:01:11.150 --> 00:01:17.100
What makes the skyscrapers here truly special is their safety and sustainability.

00:01:17.550 --> 00:01:19.450
Inside the central skyscraper,

00:01:19.750 --> 00:01:25.250
a giant tuned mass damper absorbs shock and keeps it stable in storms or quakes.

00:01:26.800 --> 00:01:31.400
Combined with an early disaster warning radar station on the roof,

00:01:31.400 --> 00:01:35.800
extreme weather is detected early to keep residents safe.

00:01:35.800 --> 00:01:40.000
Surrounding the buildings are green roofs and large parks everywhere

00:01:40.300 --> 00:01:45.600
that act as the city's natural lungs.

00:01:46.500 --> 00:01:48.800
Through this model, we want to share a simple message:

00:01:49.050 --> 00:01:55.900
a smart city isn't just about tall buildings, it's about respecting nature

00:01:56.150 --> 00:01:58.200
and using science for sustainable development.

00:01:58.700 --> 00:02:01.000
The future isn't far away.

00:02:01.300 --> 00:02:03.800
It starts with how we protect the environment today.

00:02:03.800 --> 00:02:08.000
Thank you, teacher and everyone, for listening to our presentation!
